{"headword":"אֱנָשׁ","parent_lexicon":"BDB Aramaic Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.m. man, mankind</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:10\" href=\"/Daniel.2.10\">Dn 2:10</a> +; emph. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲנָשָׁא</span> v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:38\" href=\"/Daniel.2.38\">38</a> +, so Qr <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:13\" href=\"/Daniel.4.13\">4:13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:14\" href=\"/Daniel.4.14\">14</a> (> Kt <span dir=\"rtl\">אנושׁא</span> K<sup>§ 57 f</sup>); so Nab. <span dir=\"rtl\">אנוש</span> often Lzb <sup>222</sup> Cooke <sup>219</sup> SAC <sup>22</sup>): pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲנָשִׁים</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:14\" href=\"/Daniel.4.14\">4:14</a> (Hebraism, M <sup>53*</sup> proposes <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲנָשָׁא</span>);—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>man</em>, human being, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:10\" href=\"/Daniel.2.10\">Dn 2:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 3:10\" href=\"/Daniel.3.10\">3:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:13\" href=\"/Daniel.4.13\">4:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:5\" href=\"/Daniel.5.5\">5:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:7\" href=\"/Daniel.5.7\">7</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:13\" href=\"/Daniel.6.13\">6:13</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:4\" href=\"/Daniel.7.4\">7:4</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:8\" href=\"/Daniel.7.8\">8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezra 6:11\" href=\"/Ezra.6.11\">Ezr 6:11</a>; so <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּר־אֱנָשׁ</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:13\" href=\"/Daniel.7.13\">Dn 7:13</a> <em>a son of man</em>, human being (v. especially Dr Dn 102; DB<sup>Son of Man</sup>)."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"coll. <em>men, people</em>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:11\" href=\"/Ezra.4.11\">Ezr 4:11</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:14\" href=\"/Daniel.4.14\">Dn 4:14</a> a. <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:22\" href=\"/Daniel.4.22\">22</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:29\" href=\"/Daniel.4.29\">29</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:30\" href=\"/Daniel.4.30\">30</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:21\" href=\"/Daniel.5.21\">5:21</a>, cf.pl. <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:14\" href=\"/Daniel.4.14\">4:14</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">זְרַע א׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:43\" href=\"/Daniel.2.43\">2:43</a> i.e. human off-spring; <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנֵי אֲנָשָׁא</span> <em>sons of men</em>, = men, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:38\" href=\"/Daniel.2.38\">2:38</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:21\" href=\"/Daniel.5.21\">5:21</a>."}],"num":"2."}]},"rid":"BDBA0066","strong_numbers":["606"],"next_hw":"אנשׁ²","prev_hw":"אנשׁ","all_cited":true,"quotes":[],"GK":[],"TWOT":["2591"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Aramaic Dictionary","language":"ara.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB Aramaic","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}